  "execution_contract": {
    "objective": "Q3 terminal-SOC/rolling-window boundary sensitivity and Q4 sequential four-cell dispatch-storage attribution; retain existing main models unless evidence passes the stated rules.",
    "q3_design": "Re-run the same six-region storage model and all hard audits at the current window/terminal policy plus at least two nearby native parameter settings. Record window length, terminal SOC policy, solve count/status, cost, carbon, peak, SOC bounds, simultaneous charge/discharge checks, and failed or infeasible cases.",
    "q3_acceptance": "A setting is eligible for model review only if every regional/window audit passes, no simultaneous charge/discharge occurs, SOC and grid bounds pass, and the improvement is reproducible without weakening the 269/270 audit boundary; otherwise retain the current rolling binary MILP and report the boundary.",
    "q4_design": "Construct a four-cell attribution table on the same declared scenario/window: Q2 candidate versus FIFO task envelope crossed with storage versus no-storage dispatch. Recompute costs, carbon, peak, completion and all applicable hard audits. Compute the descriptive interaction/difference-in-differences but label it sequential attribution, not causal effect.",
    "q4_acceptance": "Use the four-cell evidence to explain whether gains arise primarily from task placement, storage, or their interaction. Do not replace the current Q4 result unless all four cells are same-input, fully audited, and the alternative is no worse on the declared primary objective vector.",
    "reproducibility": "Record commands, environment, seed, input/code hashes, runtime, units, solver status and all exclusions. RegionF full-horizon LP cycling remains permanently excluded."
  }
